[06:21.48]squander [ˈskwɒndə(r)]vt. (指钱、财产等)浪费，乱花；挥 霍 例 A mechanism is being established to make it impossible for government officials to squander public money at their own will.
[06:38.88]confusion [kənˈfjuːʒn]n. 困惑，糊涂；混淆；混乱，骚乱 例 His speech flung the meeting into confusion. 搭 in confusion 乱七八糟 / throw sth. into confusion 使…陷入混乱
[06:53.40]off-season [ˌɒfˈsiːzn]n. 淡季 a. 淡季的 例 The off-season price for a standard room is about $50 a night.
