[07:19.32]goodwill [ˌɡʊdˈwɪl]n. 善意，亲切，友好；(企业的)商誉， 信誉；营业权 例 If you think that the value of any of the businesses you have acquired has gone down, you can write off some or all of that goodwill. 搭 goodwill ambassador 亲善大使，友好大使
[07:40.80]shortfall [ˈʃɔːtfɔːl]n. 不足之量；差额；亏空 例 There is a great shortfall in the supply of senior medical talents.
[07:51.48]archrival [ˌɑːkˈraɪvl]n. 主要竞争者，主要对手 例 Corporations make up Google's archrival Microsoft's traditional customer base.
